  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In the first step protonation of alcohol takes place which leads to the formation of carbocation. Ring expansion takes place in the next step. In the given process five membered ring&nbsp;become six membered ring. Now, the carbocation loses proton in the presence of potassium hydroxide to give alkene.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0039_c018b48d260b.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 490px;\" /></p>"
